{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01LDMSryU92BPUH6c73c6seb","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tsource_url: \"https://grafana.com/docs/grafana/latest/introduction/\"\n3\tfetched_at: \"2026-08-23T23:40:00-0400\"\n4\tauthority: \"Grafana Labs documentation\"\n5\tobjectives_covered: [\"D4 Observability\"]\n6\tconcepts_covered: [\"grafana\", \"dashboards\", \"visualization\", \"alerting\", \"data-sources\", \"loki\"]\n7\t---\n8\t# Grafana — Introduction (grafana.com/docs/grafana/latest/introduction/)\n9\t\n10\tGrafana is open source software that enables you to query, visualize, alert on, and explore your metrics, logs, and traces wherever they're stored. Grafana provides tools to turn your time-series database (TSDB) data into insightful graphs and visualizations. Core capabilities: dashboards (turn TSDB data into graphs and visualizations), explore (ad-hoc querying with dynamic drilldown), and alerting (send alerts through channels such as PagerDuty, Slack, and email). Grafana connects to many data sources through its plugin framework, including time-series databases such as Prometheus, SQL and NoSQL databases, log aggregation systems such as Loki, and tracing backends such as Jaeger and Tempo — bringing metrics, logs, and traces into one place.\n11\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b1daab9a-2140-4147-8700-50292188b384","uuid":"9a897405-0591-46ff-ae80-a84143652b04","timestamp":"2026-08-31T20:48:03.611Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"C:/dev/lodestar/Book-KCNA/sources/grafana-introduction-2026-08-23.md","content":"---\nsource_url: \"https://grafana.com/docs/grafana/latest/introduction/\"\nfetched_at: \"2026-08-23T23:40:00-0400\"\nauthority: \"Grafana Labs documentation\"\nobjectives_covered: [\"D4 Observability\"]\nconcepts_covered: [\"grafana\", \"dashboards\", \"visualization\", \"alerting\", \"data-sources\", \"loki\"]\n---\n# Grafana — Introduction (grafana.com/docs/grafana/latest/introduction/)\n\nGrafana is open source software that enables you to query, visualize, alert on, and explore your metrics, logs, and traces wherever they're stored. Grafana provides tools to turn your time-series database (TSDB) data into insightful graphs and visualizations. Core capabilities: dashboards (turn TSDB data into graphs and visualizations), explore (ad-hoc querying with dynamic drilldown), and alerting (send alerts through channels such as PagerDuty, Slack, and email). Grafana connects to many data sources through its plugin framework, including time-series databases such as Prometheus, SQL and NoSQL databases, log aggregation systems such as Loki, and tracing backends such as Jaeger and Tempo — bringing metrics, logs, and traces into one place.\n","numLines":11,"startLine":1,"totalLines":11}}}
