{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01UHJj9vnHVDjg8m9Hjw8hxK","type":"tool_result","content":"# OpenTelemetry Collector: Core Definition\n\n**What it is:**\n\"The OpenTelemetry Collector offers a vendor-agnostic implementation of how to receive, process and export telemetry data.\"\n\n**Key benefits:**\n- \"Removes the need to run, operate, and maintain multiple agents/collectors\"\n- \"Supports open source observability data formats (e.g. Jaeger, Prometheus, Fluent Bit, etc.)\"\n- Enables \"sending to one or more open source or commercial backends\"\n\n**Primary objectives:**\nThe Collector prioritizes usability, performance, observability, extensibility, and unification—designed as \"a single codebase, deployable as an agent or collector with support for traces, metrics, and logs.\"\n\n**When to use it:**\n\"In general we recommend using a collector alongside your service, since it allows your service to offload data quickly and the collector can take care of additional handling like retries, batching, encryption or even sensitive data filtering.\"\n\nThe documentation emphasizes that the default configuration assumes \"a local collector endpoint, so if you launch a collector it will automatically start receiving telemetry\" from language-specific instrumentation libraries."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b1daab9a-2140-4147-8700-50292188b384","uuid":"a008010b-e647-4911-97b2-d9cbc916011e","timestamp":"2026-08-31T20:48:52.543Z","tool_use_result":{"bytes":4869,"code":200,"codeText":"OK","result":"# OpenTelemetry Collector: Core Definition\n\n**What it is:**\n\"The OpenTelemetry Collector offers a vendor-agnostic implementation of how to receive, process and export telemetry data.\"\n\n**Key benefits:**\n- \"Removes the need to run, operate, and maintain multiple agents/collectors\"\n- \"Supports open source observability data formats (e.g. Jaeger, Prometheus, Fluent Bit, etc.)\"\n- Enables \"sending to one or more open source or commercial backends\"\n\n**Primary objectives:**\nThe Collector prioritizes usability, performance, observability, extensibility, and unification—designed as \"a single codebase, deployable as an agent or collector with support for traces, metrics, and logs.\"\n\n**When to use it:**\n\"In general we recommend using a collector alongside your service, since it allows your service to offload data quickly and the collector can take care of additional handling like retries, batching, encryption or even sensitive data filtering.\"\n\nThe documentation emphasizes that the default configuration assumes \"a local collector endpoint, so if you launch a collector it will automatically start receiving telemetry\" from language-specific instrumentation libraries.","durationMs":4141,"url":"https://opentelemetry.io/docs/collector/"}}
