{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_014qhZYMZVwXqQmSoLydbxGt","type":"tool_result","content":"# Context Propagation Definitions\n\n**(1) Context:**\n\"Context is an object that contains the information for the sending and receiving service, or execution unit, to correlate one signal with another.\"\n\n**(2) Propagation:**\n\"Propagation is the mechanism that moves context between services and processes.\"\n\n**(3) Context Propagation:**\n\"With context propagation, signals (traces, metrics, and logs) can be correlated with each other, regardless of where they are generated.\"\n\n**(4) Across Boundaries:**\n\"Context propagation allows traces to build causal information about a system across services that are arbitrarily distributed across process and network boundaries.\"\n\n**(5) Default Propagator:**\n\"The default propagator uses the headers specified by the W3C TraceContext specification.\"\n\n**(6) Baggage Propagation:**\n\"Baggage allows you to propagate arbitrary key-value pairs.\""}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b1daab9a-2140-4147-8700-50292188b384","uuid":"92fbbdff-a0f4-4678-bae5-b259b511b4d7","timestamp":"2026-08-31T20:49:06.618Z","tool_use_result":{"bytes":8200,"code":200,"codeText":"OK","result":"# Context Propagation Definitions\n\n**(1) Context:**\n\"Context is an object that contains the information for the sending and receiving service, or execution unit, to correlate one signal with another.\"\n\n**(2) Propagation:**\n\"Propagation is the mechanism that moves context between services and processes.\"\n\n**(3) Context Propagation:**\n\"With context propagation, signals (traces, metrics, and logs) can be correlated with each other, regardless of where they are generated.\"\n\n**(4) Across Boundaries:**\n\"Context propagation allows traces to build causal information about a system across services that are arbitrarily distributed across process and network boundaries.\"\n\n**(5) Default Propagator:**\n\"The default propagator uses the headers specified by the W3C TraceContext specification.\"\n\n**(6) Baggage Propagation:**\n\"Baggage allows you to propagate arbitrary key-value pairs.\"","durationMs":3233,"url":"https://opentelemetry.io/docs/concepts/context-propagation/"}}
