{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01VjcN3aUzrTPKNa8MyRF5mZ","type":"tool_result","content":"# The USE Method: Key Definitions\n\n**(1) What it is:**\n\"The Utilization Saturation and Errors (USE) Method is a methodology for analyzing the performance of any system.\"\n\n**(2) Definitions:**\n\n- **Utilization:** \"the average time that the resource was busy servicing work\"\n\n- **Saturation:** \"the degree to which the resource has extra work which it can't service, often queued\"\n\n- **Errors:** \"the count of error events\"\n\n**(3) What it finds:**\n\"It directs the construction of a checklist, which for server analysis can be used for quickly identifying resource bottlenecks or errors.\"\n\nAlso: \"The USE Method helps you identify which metrics to use\" and is intended \"to identify systemic bottlenecks.\"\n\n**(4) Author and origin:**\n\"I developed the USE Method to teach others how to solve common performance issues quickly, without overlooking important areas.\" The author is Brendan Gregg, as identified throughout the site."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b1daab9a-2140-4147-8700-50292188b384","uuid":"90d2689c-31cd-4057-a183-84de76cdcfa7","timestamp":"2026-08-31T20:49:45.073Z","tool_use_result":{"bytes":34405,"code":200,"codeText":"OK","result":"# The USE Method: Key Definitions\n\n**(1) What it is:**\n\"The Utilization Saturation and Errors (USE) Method is a methodology for analyzing the performance of any system.\"\n\n**(2) Definitions:**\n\n- **Utilization:** \"the average time that the resource was busy servicing work\"\n\n- **Saturation:** \"the degree to which the resource has extra work which it can't service, often queued\"\n\n- **Errors:** \"the count of error events\"\n\n**(3) What it finds:**\n\"It directs the construction of a checklist, which for server analysis can be used for quickly identifying resource bottlenecks or errors.\"\n\nAlso: \"The USE Method helps you identify which metrics to use\" and is intended \"to identify systemic bottlenecks.\"\n\n**(4) Author and origin:**\n\"I developed the USE Method to teach others how to solve common performance issues quickly, without overlooking important areas.\" The author is Brendan Gregg, as identified throughout the site.","durationMs":4476,"url":"https://www.brendangregg.com/usemethod.html"}}
