{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01P6LRAh6bGmfjsvZZ7cDhow","type":"tool_result","content":"# The RED Method: Key Definitions\n\n## The Three RED Metrics\n\nAccording to the article, the RED Method requires monitoring:\n\n- **Rate**: \"the number of requests per second\"\n- **Errors**: \"the number of those requests that are failing\"\n- **Duration**: \"the amount of time those requests take\"\n\n## Why RED Over USE\n\nTom Wilkie explained the distinction: \"The USE Method doesn't really apply to services; it applies to hardware, network disks, things like this. We really wanted a microservices-oriented monitoring philosophy, so we came up with the RED Method.\"\n\n## Creator and Timeline\n\nThe article states that Tom Wilkie \"created [the RED Method] in 2015\" after \"a new employee asked what his monitoring philosophy was.\""}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b1daab9a-2140-4147-8700-50292188b384","uuid":"9166dc40-0733-4838-b95f-6d3cfb389ca7","timestamp":"2026-08-31T20:50:15.595Z","tool_use_result":{"bytes":325416,"code":200,"codeText":"OK","result":"# The RED Method: Key Definitions\n\n## The Three RED Metrics\n\nAccording to the article, the RED Method requires monitoring:\n\n- **Rate**: \"the number of requests per second\"\n- **Errors**: \"the number of those requests that are failing\"\n- **Duration**: \"the amount of time those requests take\"\n\n## Why RED Over USE\n\nTom Wilkie explained the distinction: \"The USE Method doesn't really apply to services; it applies to hardware, network disks, things like this. We really wanted a microservices-oriented monitoring philosophy, so we came up with the RED Method.\"\n\n## Creator and Timeline\n\nThe article states that Tom Wilkie \"created [the RED Method] in 2015\" after \"a new employee asked what his monitoring philosophy was.\"","durationMs":3495,"url":"https://grafana.com/blog/the-red-method-how-to-instrument-your-services/"}}
