{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01V5ANB9RFz6rDmQqHYePZGt","type":"tool_result","content":"# Observability Definitions from CNCF Whitepaper\n\n**(1) Definition of observability for a system:**\n\"observability is a measure of how well internal states of a system can be inferred from knowledge of its external outputs.\"\n\n**(2) Observability as a system property, not a tool:**\n\"observability is not just using all the pretty and shiny tools.\"\n\n**(3) Primary signals covered:**\n\"metrics, logs, and traces\" function as the primary observability signals for most implementations.\n\n**(4) Individual signal definitions:**\n- **Metrics:** \"Metrics are numeric representations of data.\"\n- **Logs:** \"Logs are one or more textual entries describing usage patterns, activities, and operations.\"\n- **Traces:** \"Distributed tracing is the technique of understanding what happened during a distributed transaction.\"\n\n**(5) On predicting all questions in advance:**\n\"you must remember that observability is not just using all the pretty and shiny tools. You must be conscious about what outputs are coming out of your system.\""}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b1daab9a-2140-4147-8700-50292188b384","uuid":"8d2d28f8-fa97-4bb8-82c4-184699c36e46","timestamp":"2026-08-31T20:51:22.716Z","tool_use_result":{"bytes":562401,"code":200,"codeText":"OK","result":"# Observability Definitions from CNCF Whitepaper\n\n**(1) Definition of observability for a system:**\n\"observability is a measure of how well internal states of a system can be inferred from knowledge of its external outputs.\"\n\n**(2) Observability as a system property, not a tool:**\n\"observability is not just using all the pretty and shiny tools.\"\n\n**(3) Primary signals covered:**\n\"metrics, logs, and traces\" function as the primary observability signals for most implementations.\n\n**(4) Individual signal definitions:**\n- **Metrics:** \"Metrics are numeric representations of data.\"\n- **Logs:** \"Logs are one or more textual entries describing usage patterns, activities, and operations.\"\n- **Traces:** \"Distributed tracing is the technique of understanding what happened during a distributed transaction.\"\n\n**(5) On predicting all questions in advance:**\n\"you must remember that observability is not just using all the pretty and shiny tools. You must be conscious about what outputs are coming out of your system.\"","durationMs":3500,"url":"https://github.com/cncf/tag-observability/blob/main/whitepaper.md"}}
