{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01QvQj7kXNkaWm8tNnF1Gju8","type":"tool_result","content":"# Baggage in OpenTelemetry\n\n**(1) Definition:**\n\"Contextual information that is passed between signals.\" The page also notes baggage is \"a key-value store, which means it lets you propagate any data you like alongside context.\"\n\n**(2) Use cases:**\n\"Baggage is best used to include information typically available only at the start of a request further downstream.\" Examples include \"Account Identification, User IDs, Product IDs, and origin IPs.\"\n\n**(3) Propagation across services:**\n\"Baggage means you can pass data across services and processes, making it available to add to traces, metrics, or logs in those services.\"\n\n**(4) Not the same as attributes / security warning:**\n\"An important thing to note about baggage is that it is a separate key-value store and is unassociated with attributes on spans, metrics, or logs without explicitly adding them.\"\n\nAdditionally, regarding sensitive data: \"Sensitive Baggage items can be shared with unintended resources, like third-party APIs...making it visible to anyone inspecting your network traffic.\""}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b1daab9a-2140-4147-8700-50292188b384","uuid":"78a36e05-792f-4ece-a911-79ac6e420a88","timestamp":"2026-08-31T20:53:02.958Z","tool_use_result":{"bytes":3384,"code":200,"codeText":"OK","result":"# Baggage in OpenTelemetry\n\n**(1) Definition:**\n\"Contextual information that is passed between signals.\" The page also notes baggage is \"a key-value store, which means it lets you propagate any data you like alongside context.\"\n\n**(2) Use cases:**\n\"Baggage is best used to include information typically available only at the start of a request further downstream.\" Examples include \"Account Identification, User IDs, Product IDs, and origin IPs.\"\n\n**(3) Propagation across services:**\n\"Baggage means you can pass data across services and processes, making it available to add to traces, metrics, or logs in those services.\"\n\n**(4) Not the same as attributes / security warning:**\n\"An important thing to note about baggage is that it is a separate key-value store and is unassociated with attributes on spans, metrics, or logs without explicitly adding them.\"\n\nAdditionally, regarding sensitive data: \"Sensitive Baggage items can be shared with unintended resources, like third-party APIs...making it visible to anyone inspecting your network traffic.\"","durationMs":3504,"url":"https://opentelemetry.io/docs/concepts/signals/baggage/"}}
